    "background_story": "Cairo was a brilliant cryptographer with a passion for puzzles. Growing up, he was fascinated by rebuses - visual representations of words or phrases that required creative thinking to decipher. Cairo's talent for cracking codes and solving rebuses led him to work with top-secret government agencies, helping to decode encrypted messages. But his true love remained creating his own rebuses, which he shared with the world through a popular online blog. Cairo's rebuses were renowned for their cleverness and complexity, with fans and fellow puzzle enthusiasts vying to be the first to solve them. His most famous rebus, 'The Sphinx's Secret,' remained unsolved for years, until a clever teenager finally cracked the code, earning Cairo's admiration and respect.",
